{"version": "1.2.0", "run_id": "encounters-core-001", "node_id": "review-general", "launch_token": "d7a38053-c6c7-432f-89a9-27b8ce87b8d9", "bundle_sha256": "307a062f1afbed907a904aee4405114bc852796149c0fc724cdab47b18ab9533", "candidate_commit": "cf3c3bed3e9bdd3260d3018ceb534b6eaf06f4d3", "verdict": "approved", "findings": [{"severity": "P2", "message": "packages/simulation/src/encounters/step.ts: players freed within a tick (settlement returns in step 2 via settle(), respawns in step 3) are immediately eligible attackers in step 6 of the same tick, but the snapshot still holds their pre-return position (the caller only moves them after reading player-returned/player-respawned). A loser pressing on the respawn tick therefore picks a target (range, cone, line of sight) from the old encounter location, loses the 20 s respawn protection, and gets an attempt-started naming a player near a place they no longer are; the attempt then almost surely misses at landing and costs the 6 s cooldown. Draw/win returns have the same one-tick window. Neither the code nor docs/encounters.md tells the caller to suppress presses on that tick; skipping attack presses for players returned or respawned on the current tick would close it.", "disposition": "open", "worker": "encounters", "requirement": "Positions come from the snapshot; the rules never move ships."}, {"severity": "P2", "message": "packages/simulation/src/encounters/state.ts duelMarkers(): the marker's startTick is the reservation tick, not the fight's start tick (duel.startTick), and the marker stays until ledger settlement, so the elapsed time shown to others includes the 3 s+ transition and keeps running through the theft-choice window after the fight has ended. This is documented as an open assumption. It is harmless but differs from a literal 'elapsed time' of the duel.", "disposition": "open", "worker": "encounters", "requirement": "The state exposes a marker per duel for other players: position and start tick for the elapsed time, and nothing else."}, {"severity": "P2", "message": "packages/simulation/src/encounters/step.ts report validation: an end report for a duel already in phase 'fighting' is accepted with any tick >= reservedTick, including ticks before duel.startTick. Because the loser's respawn counts from end.tick, a caller bug reporting an early end tick shortens the respawn wait instead of being refused as 'invalid'.", "disposition": "open", "worker": "encounters", "requirement": "For a fight that ran, the caller reports its end: `win` (winner), `draw`, or `cancelled` (a server fault or double forfeit), with the tick it ended."}, {"severity": "P2", "message": "packages/simulation/src/encounters/modes.ts seaModeRules.separateReturn: when no pair of navigable tiles within 6 tiles is at least 3 apart, both ships are left where they were, which breaks the separation rule (documented fallback, unlikely on the slice sea). Candidates also ignore sea connectivity, so on a map with shoal walls (for example the slice sea's column-55 reef) a draw could in principle place a ship on the other side of a barrier. The minimum-cost pairing makes that rare but does not rule it out.", "disposition": "open", "worker": "encounters", "requirement": "A draw or cancellation returns both players to two distinct navigable points near the encounter position, at least 3 tiles apart and within 6 tiles, with 8 s of protection."}]}
